//! N-5, line of sight (plan §6.6): the tiles strictly between two tiles of a board, whether walls
//! block the sight between them, and from which side a target is approached.
//!
//! The line is the mirror's integer line (`HexTrait::line_to`) between the `Hex` of both tiles
//! (plan §3.5), with the game's tie rule: the lower tile index, that is the smaller row, and on
//! the same row the smaller column. It is symmetric and translation-invariant. A line one of whose
//! tiles leaves the board is `None`, never clipped (D-27): at a tie on the same row the preferred
//! tile may lie at column `−1` (R-N5-1).
//!
//! Two paths give the same result. The **table path** serves the width 15 and a distance of at
//! most 6 (the game's sight): one division, one entry of `LINES` and one product. The **loop path**
//! serves every other pair: the accumulators of `line_to`, walked on the board one direction at a
//! time, at most `W + H − 2` steps (plan §6.6, "Dispatch").
//!
//! Mirrors nothing in `hexx`: an extension (plan §6.6, N-5).

